#. official: map.1.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Where oh where can I find Princess Gwaelin?"
msgstr "O Princess... Princess Gwaelin, where art thou...?"

#. official: map.1.4.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Welcome to Tantegel Castle."
msgstr "The castle of Tantegel bids thee welcome, wanderer."

#. official: data.3.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Welcome.\n"
"We deal in tools.\n"
"What can I do for thee?"
msgstr ""
"Thou art welcome, wanderer, in this, our humble item shop.\n"
"How may we be of service to thee this day?"

#. official: map.3.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Descendant of Erdrick, listen now to my words."
msgstr "Scion of the bloodline of Erdrick, hero of legend! Long have I awaited thy coming!"

#. official: map.3.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "It is told that in ages past Erdrick fought demons with a Ball of Light."
msgstr "In days of yore, thy revered ancestor did receive of the Almighty Goddess the Sphere of Light, and by its power was our world rid of the menace which did beset it."

#. official: map.3.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Then came the Dragonlord who stole the precious globe and hid it in the darkness."
msgstr "Yet, alas, there did arise a new threat--the Dragonlord. With his cunning, he did steal away the Sphere of Light from us, plunging the land into darkness once more."

#. official: map.3.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Now, {}, thou must help us recover the Ball of Light and restore peace to our land."
msgstr "So I say unto thee, {}, vanquish the accursed Dragonlord, and reclaim the Sphere of Light!"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "The Dragonlord must be defeated."
msgstr "The accursed Dragonlord must be vanquished."

#. official: map.3.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Take now whatever thou may find in these Treasure Chests to aid thee in thy quest."
msgstr "In the chests o'er yonder wilt thou find items to aid thee on thy quest. Take what thou wilt, with my blessing."

#. official: map.3.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Then speak with the guards, for they have much knowledge that may aid thee."
msgstr "Partake thee also of the wisdom of those loyal subjects gathered here. Their knowledge will serve thee as well as any shield."

#. official: map.3.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "May the light shine upon thee, {}."
msgstr "May the Goddess guide thee to victory, brave {}!"

#. official: map.3.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"When thou art finished preparing for thy departure, please see me.\n"
"I shall wait."
msgstr ""
"Come before me once more when thou art ready to embark upon thy quest.\n"
"I shall await thy return."

#. official: map.2.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I am greatly pleased that thou hast returned, {}."
msgstr "Brave {}, thou art returned to us! Full glad am I to see thee!"

#. official: data.3.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Before reaching thy next level of experience thou must gain {} Points."
msgstr "Earn another {} points of experience, and thou shalt attain a new level."

#. official: data.3.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Before reaching thy next level of experience thou must gain {} Point."
msgstr "Earn but {} more point of experience, and thou shalt attain a new level."

#. official: data.3.7.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Will thou tell me now of thy deeds so they won't be forgotten?"
msgstr "Wilt thou record thy tale thus far in an adventure log?"

#. official: data.3.7.10
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thy deeds have been recorded on the Imperial Scrolls of Honor."
msgstr "It is written! The record is made!"

#. official: data.3.7.6
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Dost thou wish to continue thy quest?"
msgstr "Wilt thou continue on thy quest?"

#. official: data.3.7.8
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Goodbye now, {}.\n"
"'Take care and tempt not the Fates."
msgstr "May destiny bring thee before us again ere long, brave {}!"

#. official: map.2.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Death should not have taken thee, {}."
msgstr "But what is this, brave {}? Defeat doth ill become thee!"

#. official: map.2.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I will give thee another chance."
msgstr "There is naught for it--thou must be set upon thy path anew."

#. official: data.3.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "To reach the next level, thy Experience Points must increase by {}."
msgstr "Earn another {} points of experience, and thou shalt attain a new level."

#. official: data.3.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "To reach the next level, thy Experience Point must increase by {}."
msgstr "Earn but {} more point of experience, and thou shalt attain a new level."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Now, go, {}!"
msgstr "Now, go forth, brave {}!"

#. official: map.3.2.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "East of this castle is a town where armor, weapons, and many other items may be purchased."
msgstr "To the east of the castle lieth a sizeable settlement. Therein shalt thou find establishments offering weapons and armour."

#. official: map.3.2.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Return to the Inn for a rest if thou art wounded in battle, {}."
msgstr "Shouldst thou ever come to harm in battle, {}, lay thy head to rest at the inn."

#. official: map.3.2.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Sleep heals all."
msgstr "Thy wounds will be healed ere thou wakest."

#. official: map.3.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"If thou hast collected all the Treasure Chests,\n"
"a key will be found."
msgstr ""
"If thou hast partaken of the contents of each and every chest,\n"
"thou shalt by now have found a magic key."

#. official: map.3.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Once used, the key will disappear, but the door will be open and thou may pass through."
msgstr "Use thee this key to open yonder door and thou shalt lose it forever--yet use it thou must..."

#. official: data.3.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Magic keys!\n"
"They will unlock any door.\n"
"Dost thou wish to purchase one for {} GOLD?"
msgstr ""
"Hast thou need of a magic key capable of opening any door?\n"
"One such wonder will set thee back a mere {} gold coins."

#. official: map.1.8.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"We are merchants who have traveled much in this land.\n"
"Many of our colleagues have been killed by servants of the Dragonlord."
msgstr ""
"I ply the trade of the travelling merchant.\n"
"Lo, countless of our brotherhood are fallen at the hands of roaming beasts of late..."

#. official: map.1.9.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Rumor has it that entire towns have been destroyed by the Dragonlord's servants."
msgstr "They speak of a town laid to ruin by marauding monsters!"

#. official: map.1.10.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "To become strong enough to face future trials thou must first battle many foes."
msgstr "Thy first priority must ever be to hone thy skills by battling beasts."

#. official: map.1.2.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"There was a time when Brecconary was a paradise.\n"
"Then the Dragonlord's minions came."
msgstr ""
"In days of yore, the fair city of Tantegel was a veritable fairground!\n"
"And yet now, we are beset on all sides by foul fiends..."

#. official: map.1.19.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "It's a legend."
msgstr "Thus spake the foretellings of old..."

#. official: map.1.19.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "When the sun and rain meet, a Rainbow Bridge shall appear."
msgstr "When rain and sun, the twain do meet, the rain's bow shall a bridge complete."

#. official: map.1.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "King Lorik will record thy deeds in his Imperial Scroll so thou may return to thy quest later."
msgstr "If thou wouldst rejoin thy quest later, thou must needs record thy deeds in an adventure log."

#. official: map.1.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "If thou art planning to take a rest, first see King Lorik."
msgstr "If thou wouldst rest from thy quest awhile, thou must request of the King that thy deeds be recorded."

#. official: map.1.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"{}'s coming was foretold by legend.\n"
"May the light shine upon this brave warrior."
msgstr ""
"When dark doth spread across the land, light shall return by Erdrick's hand...\n"
"May the Goddess's light shine upon brave {}'s quest!"

#. official: map.14.0.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I have been waiting long for one such as thee."
msgstr "Long have we awaited the coming of one such as thee."

#. official: map.4.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Take the Treasure Chest."
msgstr "This stout chest doth house the holy Sunstone. Take it! Claim thy birthright!"

#. official: map.5.5.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "There is a town where magic keys can be purchased."
msgstr "ʼTis said that in a town far distant from this place, magic keys are sold!"

#. official: map.5.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou art most welcome in Brecconary."
msgstr "The castle town of Tantegel bids thee welcome, wanderer."

#. official: map.5.11.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Enter where thou can."
msgstr "Welcome, friend! Prithee, make thy way inside!"

#. official: map.5.6.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "If thou art cursed, come again."
msgstr "I study the removal of curses. Shouldst thou ever find thyself afflicted, prithee seek me out."

#. official: map.5.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Tell King Lorik that the search for his daughter hath failed."
msgstr "Deliver unto His Majesty the King this news... The force tasked with the rescue of Princess Gwaelin is...no more..."

#. official: map.5.7.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I am almost gone...."
msgstr "I am no more for this world..."

#. official: map.5.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Welcome! \n"
"Enter the shop and speak to its keeper across the desk."
msgstr ""
"Welcome unto thee, friend! \n"
"Prithee, make thy way inside and state thy business o'er the counter!"

#. official: map.2.1.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "{}, please save the Princess."
msgstr "Brave {}, I beg of thee! Deliver the Princess from her plight!"

#. official: map.2.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Dost thou know about Princess Gwaelin?"
msgstr "Dost thou know aught of poor Princess Gwaelin?"

#. official: map.2.1.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Half a year now hath passed since the Princess was kidnapped by the enemy."
msgstr "A half-year prior to this day, foul monsters saw fit to tear the Princess from the bosom of we, her people!"

#. official: map.2.1.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Never does the King speak of it, but he must be suffering much."
msgstr "His Majesty speaketh not of the tragedy, but ʼtis plain the loss doth pain him deeply..."

#. official: map.7.1.0
msgid "Welcome to Garinham. May thy stay be a peaceful one."
msgstr "Welcome, wanderer, to the storied settlement of Galenholm!"

#. official: map.7.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Garin, a wandering minstrel of legendary fame, is said to have built this town."
msgstr "When the great bard Galen did at last bring his wand'rings to an end, ʼtwas here that he did settle."

#. official: data.3.0.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "What dost thou wish to buy?"
msgstr "Which of our fine items tickleth thy fancy?"

#. official: data.3.0.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Please, come again."
msgstr "We shall await thy next coming most eagerly!"

#. official: data.3.1.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Is that Okay.?"
msgstr "Findest thou this price agreeable?"

#. official: data.3.0.15
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Oh, yes?\n"
"That's too bad."
msgstr ""
"Alas and alack,\n"
"a great shame indeed..."

#. official: data.3.0.5
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Sorry.\n"
"Thou hast not enough money."
msgstr ""
"Alas,\n"
"thou lackest the necessary funds, good sir!"

#. official: data.3.0.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Dost thou wish to buy anything more?"
msgstr "Might we assist thee in some other manner?"

#. official: data.3.0.13
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Then I will buy thy {} for {} GOLD."
msgstr "Then I can offer thee {1} gold coins for thy {0}."

#. official: data.3.0.14
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I thank thee."
msgstr "As ever, a thousand thanks!"

#. official: data.3.5.5
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Okay.\n"
"Good-bye, traveler."
msgstr ""
"Very well.\n"
"Fare thee well, wanderer."

#. official: data.3.5.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou hast not enough money."
msgstr "Ah... I fear thy purse will not stretch to a room, friend."

#. official: data.3.5.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Good night."
msgstr "Then may thy sleep be sound, and thy dreams pleasant..."

#. official: data.3.5.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Good morning.\n"
"Thou seems to have spent a good night."
msgstr ""
"Good morrow, friend.\n"
"I trust that thou didst sleep soundly."

#. official: data.3.5.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I shall see thee again."
msgstr "Pray, go forth with our thanks, and fare thee well."

#. official: data.3.5.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Welcome to the traveler's Inn.\n"
"Room and board is {} GOLD per night.\n"
"Dost thou want a room?"
msgstr ""
"Welcome, wanderer, unto this, our humble hostelry.\n"
"A night's lodging may be had for a mere {} gold coins.\n"
"Wilt thou lay thy weary head to rest?"

