#. official: map.33.0.7
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Thy journey is over.\n"
"Take now a long, long rest.\n"
"Hahahaha...."
msgstr ""
"Thy journey is over.\n"
"May the darkness engulf thee for all eternity!\n"
"Ha ha ha! HAHAHAHAHAAA!"

#. official: map.21.0.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Will thou take me to the castle?"
msgstr "Mighty hero, thou wilt, of course, escort me to my home, the palace?"

#. official: map.21.0.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Princess Gwaelin embraces thee.\n"
msgstr "Thou takest the Princess in thy big, strong arms.\n"

#. official: map.33.0.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"What sayest thou?\n"
"Will the great warrior stand with me?"
msgstr ""
"What say'st thou?\n"
"Wilt thou rule beside me?"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Really?"
msgstr "Thou wouldst truly rule beside me?"

#. official: map.33.0.8
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou art a fool!"
msgstr "So be it. Come, fool! Know thy insignificance!"

#. official: map.33.0.7
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Then half of this world is thine, half of the darkness, and...."
msgstr "Thou shalt receive thy just reward. This world shall be cleft in twain, and its blackest pits and dankest recesses rendered unto thee..."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "If thou dies I can bring thee back for another attempt without loss of thy deeds to date."
msgstr "Shouldst thou die, I can bring thee back for another attempt without loss of thy deeds to date."

#. official: map.2.5.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Even when we two are parted by great distances, I shall be with thee."
msgstr "My love! Though we may be apart, I am ever by thy side!"

#. official: map.16.0.6
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Thou hast no business here.\n"
"Go away."
msgstr ""
"There is no more for thee here.\n"
"Go forth unto thy destiny!"

#. official: map.14.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou hast brought the harp. Good."
msgstr "Thou art in possession of the Lyre? Very well..."

#. official: map.16.0.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Now the sun and rain shall meet and the Rainbow Drop passes to thy keeping."
msgstr "Now, at last, rain and sun shall be conjoined! Take thee the Rainbow Drop, and go forth!"

#. official: data.3.7.9
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Rest then for awhile."
msgstr "It serveth even the mighty to take pause and reflect upon their deeds from time to time."

#. official: map.9.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Dost thou still wish to go on?"
msgstr "Knowing this, art thou still resolved to face him?"

#. official: data.3.1.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I will be waiting for thy next visit."
msgstr "Thanks unto thee! May fate guide thee unto our door once more!"

#. official: data.3.1.17
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "What dost thou want?"
msgstr "And what, pray, might be thy pleasure this day?"

#. official: data.3.1.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Dost thou want anything else?"
msgstr "Is there aught else in which we might assist thee?"

#. official: data.3.1.10
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "What art thou selling?"
msgstr "Thou wouldst sell me something? And what might it be?"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Wilt thou sell anything else?"
msgstr "Wilt thou sell me aught else?"

#. official: data.3.4.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "All the best to thee."
msgstr "May the most holy on high watch over thee."

#. official: data.3.3.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I will see thee later."
msgstr "We await thy next coming with great anticipation."

#. official: data.3.5.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Good morning.\n"
"Thou hast had a good night's sleep I hope."
msgstr ""
"Good morrow, friend.\n"
"I trust that thou didst sleep soundly."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "And I would like to have something of thine--a token."
msgstr "And I would have something of thine in return--a token."

#. official: map.5.6.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I will free thee from thy curse."
msgstr "A foul curse afflicteth thee! Allow me to alleviate thy suffering!"

#. official: map.5.6.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Now, go."
msgstr "Be not afeared, friend. Thou art cursed no longer!"

#. official: map.14.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thy bravery must be proven."
msgstr "Thy foe is blessed with strength beyond reckoning. Therefore, thou must first be tested."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thus, I propose a test."
msgstr "Thus, I propose a test."

#. official: map.14.0.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "There is a Silver Harp that beckons to the creatures of the Dragonlord."
msgstr "Somewhere in this world, there is a harp unto whose melody the beasts of the wild do flock as moths to a flame."

#. official: map.14.0.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Bring this to me and I will reward thee with the Staff of Rain."
msgstr "Bring me this curious instrument, and the Staff of Rain shall be thine."

#. official: map.16.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "In thy task thou hast failed. Alas, I fear thou art not the one Erdrick predicted would save us."
msgstr "Thou hast no proof of thy birthright. Alas, I fear thou art not the one Erdrick foretold would save us."

#. official: map.16.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Go now!"
msgstr "Then begone!"

#. official: map.16.0.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou may go and search."
msgstr "Now go thee forth, and seek out sun and rain!"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Please push RESET, hold it in, then turn off the POWER."
msgstr "Please push RESET, hold it in, then turn off the POWER."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "If you turn the power off first, the Imperial Scroll of Honor containing your deeds may be lost."
msgstr "If you turn the power off first, the adventure log containing your deeds may be lost."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "BUY"
msgstr "BUY"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "SELL"
msgstr "SELL"

#. official: data.3.1.11
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou hast no possessions."
msgstr "But what is this? Thou carriest not a thing!"

#. official: data.3.0.12
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I cannot buy it."
msgstr "Alas, friend, I cannot in good conscience take such an item from thee."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I am sorry."
msgstr "Alas, I am sorry."

#. official: data.3.3.5
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I am sorry, but I cannot sell thee anymore."
msgstr "Alas, I am not permitted to sell thee any more keys at present."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I suggest making a map if thy path leads into the darkness."
msgstr "I suggest making a map if thy path leads into the darkness."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"I'm too busy.\n"
"Ask the other guard."
msgstr ""
"I'm too busy.\n"
"Ask the other guard."

#. official: map.7.8.0
msgid "The harp attracts enemies. Stay away from the grave in Garinham."
msgstr "The sound of Galen's harp is said to draw monsters from miles around. Stay away from the grave of Galen."

#. official: map.8.11.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Many believe that Princess Gwaelin is hidden away in a cave."
msgstr "A traveller did tell me of a cave at the sea's edge, in which languisheth a maiden most fair."

#. official: map.5.14.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "In legends it is said that fairies know how to put Golem to sleep."
msgstr "The tales of the ancient times do tell of towering golems laid aslumber by tiny faeries."

#. official: map.8.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "This is the village of Kol."
msgstr "Good day, friend. Thou hast found thy way to the humble village of Kol."

#. official: map.8.12.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Golem is afraid of the music of the flute, so ʼtis said."
msgstr "The towering golem feareth but one thing: the painfully pure tones of the faerie flute."

#. official: map.8.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "This bath cures rheumatism."
msgstr "Behold, the public baths! Enter, wanderer, and cleanse thyself!"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Please,save us from the minions of the Dragonlord."
msgstr "Prithee, deliver us from the Dragonlord's foul fiends."

#. official: map.5.9.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Art thou the descendant of Erdrick?\n"
"Hast thou any proof?"
msgstr ""
"Thou art of the bloodline of mighty Erdrick, thou say'st?\n"
"Hast thou proof?"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Hast thou seen Nester?\n"
"I think he may need help."
msgstr ""
"Hast thou seen Nester?\n"
"I think he may need help."

#. official: map.8.11.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "East of Hauksness there is a town, ʼtis said, where one may purchase weapons of extraordinary quality."
msgstr "East of Damdara there towereth the ramparts of proud Cantlin, wherein weapons of surpassing might are made."

#. official: map.9.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Welcome to Cantlin, the castle town."
msgstr "The impenetrable fortress of Cantlin doth bid thee welcome!"

#. official: map.9.4.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Come buy my radishes! They are fresh and cheap.\n"
"Buy thy radishes today!"
msgstr ""
"Welcome, friend, welcome! If thou likest carrots, thou hast come to the right place!\n"
"Buy thy carrots today!"

#. official: map.9.5.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "What shall I get for thy dinner?"
msgstr "Hmm... What to prepare, I wonder..."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"I'm Nester.\n"
"Hey, where am I? No, don't tell me!"
msgstr ""
"I'm Nester.\n"
"A pox on my memory! Where am I? No, don't tell me!"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I know nothing."
msgstr "I know nothing."

#. official: map.9.17.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "To learn how proof may be obtained that thy ancestor was the great Erdrick, see a man in this very town."
msgstr "If thou wand'rest in search of proof of thy lineage, see a man in this very town."

#. official: map.9.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Grandfather used to say that his friend, Wynn, had buried something of great value at the foot of a tree behind his shop."
msgstr "My father's father spoke of his friend Magog, and of a great treasure which he did bury beneath the tree behind his shop..."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "ʼTis said that Erdrick's sword could cleave steel."
msgstr "ʼTis said that the Sword of Erdrick could cleave steel."

#. official: map.9.19.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "My Grandfather Wynn once had a shop on the east side of Hauksness."
msgstr "My grandfather, Magog, did once tend a shop in the east of the desert town of Damdara."

#. official: map.2.5.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Dost thou love me, {}?"
msgstr "{}... Thinkest thou often of thy beloved princess?"

#. official: map.9.3.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou art truly brave."
msgstr "Verily, thou art a hero indeed!"

#. official: map.9.3.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"That is good.’\n"
"`No one will say thou art afraid."
msgstr ""
"Well, mayhap ʼtis for the best.’\n"
"`The hero who goeth blithely to his certain doom is but a heroical fool."

#. official: data.3.1.7
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou cannot hold more Herbs."
msgstr "Alas, thou already bearest all the medicinal herbs a man might carry..."

#. official: data.3.1.13
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Thou said the {}.\n"
"I will buy thy {} for {} GOLD.\n"
"Is that all right?"
msgstr ""
"The {}, thou say'st?\n"
"Pray, permit me a moment to consider thy {}...\n"
"Would {} gold coins suffice?"

#. official: data.3.4.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Will thou buy some Fairy Water for {} GOLD to keep the Dragonlord's minions away?"
msgstr "Might a phial of holy water with the power to repel foul beasts interest thee? At a mere {} gold coins, surely it must?"

#. official: data.3.4.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou cannot carry anymore."
msgstr "Hm? Thy burden is too great already. Pray, lighten thy load and come unto me once more."

#. official: data.3.4.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"I thank thee.\n"
"Won't thou buy one more bottle?"
msgstr ""
"Thanks unto thee, friend.\n"
"Another phial, perhaps?"

#. official: data.3.3.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Here,take this key.\n"
"Dost thou wish to purchase more?"
msgstr ""
"Excellent. I present unto thee one magic key.\n"
"Desirest thou another?"

#. official: map.2.8.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"I am glad thou hast returned.\n"
"All our hopes are riding on thee."
msgstr ""
"Thou art returned to us! Full glad am I!\n"
"If it be in the power of any man to deliver us from the Dragonlord's tyranny, that man is surely thee!"

#. official: data.3.7.11
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "See me again when thy level has increased."
msgstr "When thy level groweth greater, come before me and record thine adventure."

#. official: map.2.6.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Now, Gwaelin, come to my side."
msgstr "Come now, Gwaelin. Return thee to thy rightful place at my side."

#. official: map.5.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Beware the bridges!"
msgstr "Wherever the path of adventure leadeth thee, beware of bridges!"

#. official: map.5.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Danger grows when thou crosses."
msgstr "For verily, beyond each bridge wilt thou find ever more fierce and fearsome beasts!"

#. official: map.8.10.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou shouldst come here again."
msgstr "Seek out the sword of thine ancestor, and come here again."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Dreadful is the South Island."
msgstr "Dreadful is the isle to the south."

#. official: map.8.9.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Great strength and skill and wit only will bring thee back from that place."
msgstr "ʼTis said that land is rife with beasts of incomparable ferocity! Only great strength and skill and wit will bring thee back."

#. official: map.9.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "ʼTis said that the Dragonlord hath claws that can cleave iron and fiery breath that can melt stone."
msgstr "The claws of the Dragonlord rendeth steel as if ʼtwere parchment, while his breath melteth stone as if ʼtwere ice."

#. official: map.9.2.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "It is said that many have held Erdrick's armor."
msgstr "The legends do tell that the armour of mighty Erdrick was passed down from hand to hand..."

#. official: map.9.2.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "The last to have it was a fellow named Wynn."
msgstr "Until it came finally into the hand of one who bore the name of Magog..."

#. official: map.1.16.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Let us wish the warrior well!"
msgstr "Let us pray for the success of this, our hero!"

#. official: map.1.16.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "May the light be thy strength!"
msgstr "May the light of the heavens shine upon thee..."

#. official: map.9.18.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "From Tantegel Castle travel 70 leagues to the south and 40 to the east."
msgstr "From Tantegel Castle travel 70 paces to the south and 40 paces to the east."

#. official: map.21.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I am Gwaelin, daughter of Lorik."
msgstr "At long last! Brave hero, I am Gwaelin, Princess of Tantegel."

#. official: map.33.0.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I give thee now a chance to share this world and to rule half of it if thou will now stand beside me."
msgstr "Come! Take thy rightful place at my side! Do so, and I will grant unto thee dominion over half this world!"

#. official: map.2.6.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Gwaelin then whispers:\n"
"`Wait a moment,please.\n"
"I would give a present to {}.’"
msgstr ""
"Princess Gwaelin then whispers:\n"
"`I shall, Father--but first I must give brave {} a token of my undying... appreciation!’"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Please give me thy {}."
msgstr "Pray, give me thy {}."

#. official: map.2.1.4
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Oh, brave {}."
msgstr "Brave {}! Beloved saviour and hero of the people!"

#. official: map.1.2.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thank you for saving the Princess."
msgstr "Zounds! Praise be! The Princess is saved! Thou art a hero indeed, friend!"

#. official: map.5.7.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Who touches me?’\n"
"`I see nothing, nor can I hear."
msgstr ""
"Who...? Who toucheth now mine hand?’\n"
"`I see not... I hear not... I am no more for this world..."

#. official: map.2.0.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Forever shall I be grateful for the gift of my daughter returned to her home, {}.\n"
"Accept my thanks."
msgstr ""
"Brave {}--thou didst deliver my beloved daughter from her plight, and return her safely unto me.\n"
"I shall not forget this great gift."

#. official: map.2.6.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Please accept my love, {}."
msgstr "Brave {}! Pray accept this modest symbol of mine affection, humble though it may be!"

#. official: map.2.6.3
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Farewell, {}."
msgstr "Now, brave {}, go forth upon thy quest!"

#. official: map.8.10.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Though thou art as brave as thy ancestor, {}, thou cannot defeat the great Dragonlord with such weapons."
msgstr "Brave {}, bearer of the blood of Erdrick! Know that thy weapon will not serve to vanquish the Dragonlord!"

#. official: map.21.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou art brave indeed to rescue me, {}."
msgstr "At long last! One has come who will deliver me from my plight! Brave {}!"

#. official: map.33.0.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Welcome, {}.\n"
"I am the Dragonlord--King of Kings."
msgstr ""
"So, thou art come before me at last, {}!\n"
"I am the Dragonlord, master of masters, king of kings!"

#. official: data.3.1.9
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"The {}?\n"
"Thank you very much."
msgstr ""
"The {}?\n"
"With our humblest compliments!"

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Oh, my dearest Gwaelin!’\n"
"`I hate thee, {}."
msgstr ""
"Oh, my dearest Gwaelin!’\n"
"`A pox upon thee, {}!"

msgid "H: Show Controls"
msgstr "H: Show Controls"

msgid "F11: Toggle Fullscreen"
msgstr "F11: Toggle Fullscreen"

msgid "1-5: Adjust Game Speed"
msgstr "1-5: Adjust Game Speed"

