msgid ""
"Game set to {}x speed.\n"
"({} FPS)"
msgstr ""
"Game set to {}x speed.\n"
"({} FPS)"

#. official: data.3.7.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Thou art strong enough!\n"
"Why can thou not defeat the Dragonlord?"
msgstr ""
"Thou art more than mighty enough to face the Dragonlord!\n"
"Go forth unto certain victory!"

#. official: map.8.16.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Hast thou found the flute?"
msgstr "Is the fabled faerie flute perhaps in thy possession already?"

#. official: map.8.9.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Hast thou been to the southern island?"
msgstr "Hast thou set foot upon the isle to the south of this place?"

#. official: map.6.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Hast thou found a magic temple?"
msgstr "Hast thou happened yet upon that most holy of shrines?"

#. official: map.6.8.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Is that a wedding ring?’\n"
"`Thou seems too young to be married."
msgstr ""
"Is that a ring I spy upon thy finger, friend?’\n"
"`Thou seemest too young to be married."

#. official: map.6.8.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "All true warriors wear a ring."
msgstr "To wear a ring is prudent, even for a mighty warrior."

#. official: map.1.13.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Thou must have a key to open a door."
msgstr "No door may be opened without a key."

#. official: map.1.17.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "If thy Hit Points are high enough, by all means, enter."
msgstr "If thou hast the utmost faith in thy physical hardiness, by all means, enter."

#. official: map.1.5.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "When entering the cave, take with thee a torch."
msgstr "If thou questeth in caves or dungeons dank, a torch or two will serve thee well, friend."

#. official: map.1.18.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"In Garinham,look for the grave of Garin.\n"
"Thou must push on a wall of darkness there."
msgstr ""
"Get thee to Galenholm, and look for the grave of Galen.\n"
"There press thee 'pon the wall of darkness till the path groweth clear."

#. official: map.1.14.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"I am looking for the castle cellar.\n"
"I heard it is not easily found."
msgstr ""
"A pox on my memory!\n"
"I could have sworn that the castle dungeon was around here somewhere..."

#. official: map.5.8.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Some say that Garin's grave is home to a Silver Harp."
msgstr "They say great Galen took his beloved lyre unto his grave."

#. official: map.5.13.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Watch thy Hit Points when in the Poisonous Marsh."
msgstr "Beware the poisonous marshes, friend... Cross them only when thou art in full good health."

#. official: map.5.4.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Go north to the seashore, then follow the coastline west until thou hath reached Garinham."
msgstr "Fair Galenholm is far to the north of here, and west along the coast."

#. official: data.3.7.11
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "See King Lorik when thy experience levels are raised."
msgstr "When thy level groweth greater, go before the King."

#. official: map.5.10.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "No,I am not Princess Gwaelin."
msgstr "Nay, nay! Thou art mistaken! I am not the fair Princess Gwaelin!"

#. official: map.7.8.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"The harp attracts enemies.\n"
"Stay away from the grave in Garinham."
msgstr ""
"The sound of Galen's harp is said to draw monsters from miles around.\n"
"Stay away from the grave of Galen."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"I hate people!\n"
"Go! Leave me!"
msgstr ""
"I hate people!\n"
"Go! Leave me!"

#. official: map.7.9.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Once there was a town called Hauksness far to the south,but I do not know if it still exists."
msgstr "Oft did I lay my head at the inn of fair Damdara in the south. I wonder if it stands still..."

#. official: map.7.8.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "They say that Erdrick's armor was hidden long ago."
msgstr "Wand'ring merchants do tell that the armour of mighty Erdrick surviveth to this day somewhere in the land."

#. official: map.7.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Welcome to Garinham.\n"
"May thy stay be a peaceful one."
msgstr ""
"Welcome, wanderer,\n"
"to the storied settlement of Galenholm!"

#. official: map.7.4.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "It is said that the Princess was kidnapped and taken eastward."
msgstr "The foul fiends that did bear off the Princess Gwaelin flew eastward. Ever eastward..."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"I have heard of one named Nester.\n"
"Dost thou know such a one?"
msgstr ""
"I have heard of one named Nester.\n"
"Dost thou know such a one?"

#. official: map.8.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Rimuldar is the place to buy keys."
msgstr "Know'st thou of Rimuldar? I hear a merchant there doth ply a trade in keys!"

#. official: map.6.14.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I am Orwick, and I am waiting for my girl friend."
msgstr "I am Orwick. Where art thou, my love? And wherefore art thou so very tardy?"

#. official: map.5.11.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Welcome!"
msgstr "Welcome, friend!"

#. official: map.6.11.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Who art thou?\n"
"Leave at once or I will call my friends."
msgstr ""
"Who art thou!? What business hast thou here!?\n"
"Begone, lest I call the guard!"

#. official: map.6.0.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Welcome to the town of Rimuldar."
msgstr "Thou art come unto the town of Rimuldar, stranger. We bid thee welcome."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "The scales of the Dragonlord are as hard as steel."
msgstr "The scales of the Dragonlord are as hard as steel."

#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"No, I have no tomatoes.\n"
"I have no tomatoes today."
msgstr ""
"No, I have no tomatoes.\n"
"I have no tomatoes today."

#. official: map.6.18.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Thou shalt find the Stones of Sunlight in Tantegel Castle,\n"
"if thou has not found them yet."
msgstr "The legends speak of a stone betokening the sun which doth slumber within the keep of Tantegel's castle."

#. official: map.6.5.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Before long the enemy will arrive."
msgstr "Doubt not that the fiends are coming. Our town too will surely be laid waste ere long..."

#. official: map.5.4.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Heed my warning! Travel not to the south for there the monsters are fierce and terrible."
msgstr "South of this place wilt thou encounter fiends yet more fearsome even than those that do roam these parts!"

#. official: map.6.14.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Good day,I am Howard. Four steps south of the bath in Kol thou shalt find a magic item."
msgstr "Good day, I am Howard. From the baths of Kol, walk thee four paces south. There shalt thou find a true treasure."

#. official: map.6.6.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "In this world is there any sword that can pierce the scales of the Dragonlord?"
msgstr "Can there truly exist any weapon mighty enough to slay the Dragonlord?"

#. official: map.6.13.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Orwick is late again. I'm starving."
msgstr "Oh, Orwick! What art thou about? Wherefore tarry'st thou so? I'm starving."

#. official: map.8.16.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Go to the town of Cantlin."
msgstr "Then make haste unto the city of Cantlin--there wilt thou find out its use!"

#. official: map.8.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Howard had it, but he went to Rimuldar and never returned."
msgstr "Howard had it, but he went to Rimuldar, and hath yet to return."

#. official: map.8.9.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "I have heard that powerful enemies live there."
msgstr "But ʼtis said that land is rife with beasts of incomparable ferocity!"

#. official: map.8.9.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "To the south, I believe, there is a town called Rimuldar."
msgstr "ʼTis famed for the town of Rimuldar, which standeth proudly upon it."

#. official: map.6.7.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "In this temple do the sun and rain meet."
msgstr "There shall rain and sun, the twain meet at last..."

#. official: map.6.7.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Go to the south."
msgstr "Then journey thee south from this place. There shalt thou find it."

#. official: map.5.2.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Many have been the warriors who have perished on this quest."
msgstr "Many a courageous young adventurer hath set forth from Tantegel town. Alas, nary a one of them hath returned."

#. official: map.5.12.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Within sight of Tantegel Castle to the south is Charlock,"
msgstr "To the south, within sight of Tantegel Castle, there lieth a great fortress shrouded in mist,"

#. official: map.5.12.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "The fortress of the Dragonlord."
msgstr "The Dragonlord's Castle."

#. official: map.6.9.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Over the western part of this island Erdrick created a rainbow."
msgstr "Legends tell of how mighty Erdrick did use the rain's bow as a bridge to reach the forsaken isle."

#. official: map.6.9.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "ʼTis also said that he entered the darkness from a hidden entrance in the room of the Dragonlord."
msgstr "They speak also of how he did descend into the darkness through a hidden doorway in the throne room of his foe."

#. official: map.6.7.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "This is a magic place."
msgstr "Thou art come unto a place of foretelling... Of sight beyond sight."

#. official: map.8.10.1
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Finally thou hast obtained it, {}."
msgstr "So, thou hast recovered the Sword of Erdrick at long last, brave {}."

#. official: map.4.1.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"You are {}?\n"
"It has been long since last we met."
msgstr ""
"Thou art {}, art thou not?\n"
"Thou art the very spit of thy storied forebear."

#. official: map.3.0.2
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "A word of advice."
msgstr "I would fain furnish thee with such counsel as may be of use on thy quest."

#. official: map.2.2.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "Save thy money for more expensive armor."
msgstr "When thou hast accrued sufficient funds, thou wouldst be well advised to purchase better weapons and armour."

#. official: map.2.3.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid ""
"Listen to what people say.\n"
"It can be of great help."
msgstr ""
"No hero should ever deem himself too busy to engage in idle conversation.\n"
"Naught is e'er as trivial as it may seem..."

#. official: map.1.15.0
#: data/text/dialog_lookup_table.py
msgid "But for thee I wish success, {}."
msgstr "I shall remain here and pray for thy success, {}."

